    <bpmn:process id="W_W4972" name="W4972. Load Securement, Weight Distribution &amp; Vehicle Overload Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: During/after loading (W4970); vehicle suitability check (W4968)
Frequency: Per bulky load × 200 stores
Volume: ~7–10 bulky loads requiring securement per store per day × 200 stores (all bulky loads are secured per W4970)
Owner: Loading-Zone Supervisor / Loaders
Participants: Loaders, Forklift Operators (W4969), Store Ops (VS-07), Customer Safety (VS-147), Calibration (VS-115)
Source: workflow W4972 — Load Securement, Weight Distribution &amp; Vehicle Overload Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4972_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4972_Lane1" name="Loader">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4972_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4972_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4972_Lane2" name="Loaders">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4972_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4972_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4972_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4972_Start4" name="During/after loading (W4970); vehicle suitability check (W4968)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4972_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4972_Task5" name="Plan weight distribution &amp; load order: distribute weight across the vehicle…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Plan weight distribution &amp; load order: distribute weight across the vehicle axles, place heavy items low/forward, balance side-to-side, and stay within the vehicle&#x27;s payload/load rating (links W4968 suitability)
Responsible (R): Loader / Supervisor
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per load</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4972_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4972_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4972_Task6" name="Secure the load: strap/tie-down/chock/block the cargo…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Secure the load: strap/tie-down/chock/block the cargo (lumber/tile/cement/appliance), verify securement points and strap rating, and prevent shift/rollover in transit (links VS-147 — load-shift injury/liability)
Responsible (R): Loaders / Supervisor
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per load</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4972_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4972_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4972_Task7" name="Prevent overload &amp; advise the customer: weigh/estimate the load (links VS-115…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Prevent overload &amp; advise the customer: weigh/estimate the load (links VS-115 scales for catch-weight/bulk), refuse unsafe overload (offer delivery VS-06/VS-143 or larger rental VS-162), advise the customer on safe transport/securement, and document
Responsible (R): Loaders / Supervisor / CX
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per load</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4972_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4972_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4972_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4972_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4972_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-744 (ensure controlled execution — Bulky-Goods Loading, Forklift-in-Customer-Area &amp; Vehicle Coordination (PA-171.2).) | - CTL-744: weight distribution planned; load secured to rating; overload refused; customer advised; documented
Owner: Loading-Zone Supervisor / Loaders</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4972_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4972_Annotation9" targetRef="W4972_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
