    <bpmn:process id="W_W4975" name="W4975. Bulk Material Breaking, Handling &amp; Yard-to-Vehicle Transfer" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Bulk material pickup (cement, lumber, sand/gravel, nails bulk, catch-weight)
Frequency: Continuous × 200 stores
Volume: ~5–10 bulk-breaking events per store per week × 200 stores
Owner: Yard Lead / Loading-Zone Supervisor / Store Ops
Participants: Yard Staff, Loaders, Forklift Operators (W4969), Calibration (VS-115), Inventory (VS-05)
Source: workflow W4975 — Bulk Material Breaking, Handling &amp; Yard-to-Vehicle Transfer</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4975_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4975_Lane1" name="Yard Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4975_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4975_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4975_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4975_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4975_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4975_Start3" name="Bulk material pickup (cement, lumber, sand/gravel, nails bulk, catch-weight)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4975_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4975_Task4" name="Break bulk &amp; measure: break bulk stock (cement bags from pallet, lumber…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Break bulk &amp; measure: break bulk stock (cement bags from pallet, lumber board-foot cut, catch-weight nails/wire — links VS-09.1 W951 bulk breaking, VS-115 scales), measure/weigh accurately, and stage for the customer
Responsible (R): Yard Staff / Loaders
Accountable (A): Yard Lead
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4975_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4975_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4975_Task5" name="Transfer yard-to-vehicle: move the broken/measured bulk to the customer vehicle…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Transfer yard-to-vehicle: move the broken/measured bulk to the customer vehicle (manual or forklift W4969), with the spotter (W4971) and securement (W4972), and update inventory on the break (links VS-05)
Responsible (R): Yard Staff / Loaders / Operator
Accountable (A): Yard Lead
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4975_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4975_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4975_Task6" name="Reconcile &amp; document: reconcile the broken/measured quantity to the sale (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reconcile &amp; document: reconcile the broken/measured quantity to the sale (links VS-08 catch-weight, VS-115 calibration), document the break/transfer, and feed inventory accuracy (VS-05.1)
Responsible (R): Yard Staff / Inventory / Calibration
Accountable (A): Yard Lead
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4975_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4975_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4975_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4975_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4975_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-744 (ensure controlled execution — Bulky-Goods Loading, Forklift-in-Customer-Area &amp; Vehicle Coordination (PA-171.2).) | - CTL-744: calibrated scales (VS-115); break posted to inventory; quantity reconciled to sale; safe handling
Owner: Yard Lead / Loading-Zone Supervisor / Store Ops</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
