    <bpmn:process id="W_W4976" name="W4976. Hazardous / Fragile / High-Value Goods Loading Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Pickup of DG/hazmat, fragile, or high-value goods
Frequency: Event-driven × 200 stores
Volume: ~5–10 DG/fragile/high-value pickups per store per week × 200 stores
Owner: Loading-Zone Supervisor / HSE (VS-24) / LP (VS-23)
Participants: Loaders, HSE (VS-24), LP (VS-23), DG Compliance (VS-114), Store Ops (VS-07)
Source: workflow W4976 — Hazardous / Fragile / High-Value Goods Loading Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4976_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4976_Lane1" name="Loaders">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4976_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4976_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4976_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4976_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4976_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4976_Start3" name="Pickup of DG/hazmat, fragile, or high-value goods">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4976_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4976_Task4" name="Apply the goods-specific loading protocol: DG/hazmat (paint/solvent/gas…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Apply the goods-specific loading protocol: DG/hazmat (paint/solvent/gas cylinder/LPG — links VS-114 DG compliance, segregation/securement/ventilation); fragile (glass, ceramic, appliance — protection/orientation); high-value (power tools, copper — LP oversight VS-23)
Responsible (R): Loaders / HSE / LP
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4976_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4976_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4976_Task5" name="Load safely per protocol: segregate incompatible DG, secure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Load safely per protocol: segregate incompatible DG, secure cylinders/fragile/high-value, prevent damage/leak/theft, advise the customer on transport (DG restrictions, fragile handling), and document
Responsible (R): Loaders / HSE / LP
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4976_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4976_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4976_Task6" name="Comply &amp; report: ensure DG customer-handoff compliance (links VS-114)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Comply &amp; report: ensure DG customer-handoff compliance (links VS-114), high-value release controls (links VS-23), and incident/leak/damage reporting (VS-24/VS-114/VS-147)
Responsible (R): Loaders / HSE / LP
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor / HSE Lead
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4976_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4976_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4976_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4976_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4976_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-744 (ensure controlled execution — Bulky-Goods Loading, Forklift-in-Customer-Area &amp; Vehicle Coordination (PA-171.2).) | - CTL-744: goods-specific protocol applied; DG segregated/secured; fragile protected; high-value LP-controlled; incidents reported
Owner: Loading-Zone Supervisor / HSE (VS-24) / LP (VS-23)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
